\emph{Step 5 (the extension).} Off the origin $\partial^{2}(L_{\mu}/s) = -4/s^{2}$ (computed), so $s^{-2} = - rac14\partial^{2}(L_{\mu}/s)$, and $L_{\mu}/s$ is locally integrable (the identity of differential renormalisation \cite{FreedmanJohnsonLatorre1992}). Define $ ar\Pi$ as in the statement, all derivatives distributional. On $x 
